        example:
          "For roughly two decades after the calendar reform, French voters typically gave newly elected presidents a supportive parliamentary majority in the legislative elections that followed within weeks. Macron's decision to dissolve the National Assembly and call snap legislative elections in June 2024, after his own party's poor European Parliament result, produced instead a fragmented, three-bloc Assembly with no majority for any single camp, a dramatic real-time illustration of just how thoroughly the fait majoritaire pattern has broken down.",
