        example:
          "The 2017 runoff between Macron and Le Pen saw blank and null ballots reach roughly 12% of votes cast, a historically high total widely read as reflecting significant discomfort with both finalists even among voters who turned out specifically to register that discomfort rather than stay home. Far-left leader Jean-Luc Mélenchon notably declined to explicitly endorse Macron over Le Pen in both 2017 and 2022, instead urging voters simply not to give a single vote to the far right while stopping short of a direct vote-Macron endorsement, a calibrated position that implicitly left the vote blanc option open for supporters unwilling to actively back either finalist.",
